cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "SmartAgri core: active, uncertainty-aware agronomic advisory"
abstract: >-
  Open core of an agronomic advisory system for maize. Before any text is generated, explicit deterministic layers
  decide whether the system may advise on a parcel at all: applicability of knowledge passages, quality of each
  input, sufficiency of the inputs, choice of the next question and a decision policy that recommends, gives a
  conditional answer, asks or abstains. Agronomic numbers are computed in code (FAO-56 ETc = Kc x ET0, a simplified
  root-zone balance, gross depth = net / efficiency), and grounding checks keep a language model, when one is used,
  from adding unsupported numbers or sentences. The repository includes BM25 retrieval with optional dense ranking,
  a web app, and an evaluation harness with an ablation ladder, blind rating, a leakage guard and a protocol lock.
  Configuration values and the corpus are development defaults pending agronomic review.
